{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"n0","type":"text","text":"## Hinge #3: Yahweh-El Distinction\n\nYahweh and El were originally distinct deities\nwho became amalgamated. Yahweh was a foreign\nimport from the south, later grafted onto the\nCanaanite high god El.\n\n**Day | HIGH | 65 dependents across 4 levels**\n\n[[notes/synthesis/phase2-cascade-trees]]\n[[notes/synthesis/phase1-hinge-inventory]]","x":-2357,"y":-4480,"width":360,"height":360,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"n2","type":"text","text":"## Asherah Appears as a Goddess\n\nAsherah appears as a GODDESS in five OT\npassages — not just a cult object. Later\nredactors suppressed this.\n\n**Day | HIGH | ⚠️ contra:1 chall:1**","x":-2637,"y":-3680,"width":280,"height":280,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"n18","type":"text","text":"## 🔴 CRITICAL: Monotheism Born in Exile\n\nTrue monotheism — other gods do not EXIST —\nemerged in the Babylonian exile, first\narticulated in Second Isaiah (Isa 45:5).\n\n**Romer | VERY-HIGH | chall:6**","x":-4400,"y":-2170,"width":280,"height":330,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"n3","type":"text","text":"## Three-Stage Convergence Model\n\n(1) El as original god → (2) Yahweh\nidentified with El → (3) El's traits\nabsorbed into Yahweh's identity.\n\n**Smith | MEDIUM-HIGH | ⚠️ chall:3**","x":-4000,"y":-4250,"width":280,"height":290,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"n15","type":"text","text":"## National Theology Pre-Monotheism\n\nBefore monotheistic rhetoric, Israel had\na \"national theology\" — Yahweh was Israel's\npatron god among many.\n\n**Smith | HIGH | ⚠️ contra:1**","x":-4800,"y":-3370,"width":280,"height":285,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"n20","type":"text","text":"## Empires Made National-God Obsolete\n\nThe rise of Neo-Assyrian and Babylonian\nempires demanded a super-national god —\nnational theology became untenable.\n\n**Smith | HIGH | ⚠️ chall:1**","x":-5560,"y":-2720,"width":280,"height":320,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"n23","type":"text","text":"## Lineage Erosion → Divine Family Unstable\n\n8th-6th c. BCE lineage system erosion\nmade the divine family metaphor structurally\nunstable — monotheism filled the vacuum.\n\n**Smith | LOW-MEDIUM**","x":-5280,"y":-1400,"width":280,"height":320,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"n5","type":"text","text":"## Golden Calves Were Yahwistic\n\nJeroboam's golden calves were Yahwistic\nimages (not Baal, not pedestals) derived\nfrom El's bull iconography.\n\n**Day | HIGH | ⚠️ contra:1 chall:2**","x":-2277,"y":-3200,"width":280,"height":320,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"n22","type":"text","text":"## New Creation: Divine-Human Fusion\n\nRevelation 21-22 = final fusion of divine\nand human realms — ultimate reversal of\nthe Babel disinheritance.\n\n**Heiser | MEDIUM**","x":-3220,"y":57,"width":280,"height":263,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"n9","type":"text","text":"## Babel: Nations to Divine Beings\n\nAt Babel, God assigned nations to lesser\n*elohim* — Yahweh kept Israel as His own\ninheritance (Deut 32:8-9 LXX/DSS).\n\n**Heiser | MEDIUM | ⚠️ contra:2**","x":-2940,"y":-570,"width":280,"height":290,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"n16","type":"text","text":"## 🔴 CRITICAL: Polytheism Everywhere\n\nIsraelite religion was everywhere and\nalways polytheistic in practice until\nthe very end of the monarchy.\n\n**Dever | HIGH | contra:4 chall:1**","x":-4280,"y":1040,"width":280,"height":360,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"n14","type":"text","text":"## Golden Calves at Dan & Bethel\n\nThe calves were legitimate Yhwh symbols\nusing traditional El/Baal bull imagery —\nnot apostate worship.\n\n**Romer | MEDIUM-HIGH**","x":-1997,"y":-2340,"width":280,"height":335,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"n17","type":"text","text":"## 🔴 CRITICAL: Monotheism = Elite Fiction\n\nMonotheism was a late, elite construction —\na \"book religion\" written by the few for\nthe few that never displaced folk practice.\n\n**Dever | HIGH | contra:3 chall:2**","x":-1040,"y":1210,"width":280,"height":310,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"n1","type":"text","text":"## \"Israel\" Is an El Name\n\nThe name \"Israel\" is an El name, not a\nYhwh name — the group originally venerated\nEl and adopted Yahweh later.\n\n**Romer | HIGH**","x":-1040,"y":-3850,"width":280,"height":340,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"n11","type":"text","text":"## Yhwh Not Jerusalem's Original God\n\nYhwh rose to supremacy gradually,\ncompeting with and absorbing other\ndeities — he was a late arrival.\n\n**Romer | HIGH**","x":-900,"y":-2510,"width":280,"height":255,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"n6","type":"text","text":"## Asherah Was Yhwh's Consort\n\nAsherah was El's consort at Ugarit and\nbecame Yhwh's consort in Israel when\nYahweh absorbed El's identity.\n\n**Romer | HIGH | ⚠️ contra:1 chall:3**","x":-3220,"y":-3370,"width":280,"height":290,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"schmid-zone","type":"text","text":"## Schmid Threat Zone\n\n**59% of graph's evidential foundation at risk\nif Pentateuch is Persian-period (Schmid 2023).**\n\nIf Pentateuch dates to Persian era rather than\nIron II, the entire textual basis for the Yahweh-El\ndistinction timeline collapses.\n\nThe cascade assumes Iron II composition dates for\ntexts preserving older polytheistic strata. Persian\ndating flips the argument: \"preserved older theology\"\nbecomes \"theological retrojection.\"\n\n[[notes/synthesis/phase3-counter-position-stress-tests]]\n[[notes/synthesis/capstone-what-does-this-mean]]","x":-4100,"y":-3370,"width":380,"height":570,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"n10","type":"text","text":"## Deut 32:8-9 Preserves Older Theology\n\nPsalm 82 and Deut 32:8-9 preserve an\nOLDER theology where Yahweh was originally\nsubordinate to Elyon (the Most High = El).\n\n**Smith | HIGH**","x":-3580,"y":-2005,"width":280,"height":335,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"n21","type":"text","text":"## Divine Family = Conceptual Unity\n\nThe divine family model gave polytheism\nstructural flexibility — outsiders integrated\nthrough marriage and adoption metaphors.\n\n**Smith | MEDIUM-HIGH | ⚠️ contra:1**","x":-3860,"y":-60,"width":280,"height":316,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"n4","type":"text","text":"## Divine Council from Ugaritic\n\nThe OT \"sons of God\" derive directly\nfrom the Ugaritic concept of El's\nheavenly court and council.\n\n**Day | VERY-HIGH | ⚠️ chall:3**","x":-2917,"y":-1040,"width":280,"height":170,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"n19","type":"text","text":"## Biblical Yahwism = Dtr Fiction\n\nThe biblical picture of pure Yahwism is\na Deuteronomistic fiction; the real cult\nwas thoroughly polytheistic.\n\n**Romer | HIGH**","x":-1320,"y":110,"width":280,"height":290,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"n13","type":"text","text":"## Four-Tier Ugaritic Pantheon\n\n(1) Presiding couple (El + Athirat)\n(2) Major deities (3) Craftsmen/messengers\n(4) Servants. Israel inherited the structure.\n\n**Smith | MEDIUM-HIGH**","x":-3860,"y":-1280,"width":280,"height":325,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"n12","type":"text","text":"## Psalm 82: Yahweh Prosecutes Gods\n\nYahweh prosecutes the gods for judicial\nfailure in the divine council — they will\n\"die like men\" (Ps 82:7).\n\n**Lewis | HIGH | ⚠️ contra:3**","x":-1717,"y":-740,"width":280,"height":255,"color":"4"}
	],
